938-
939:## Wave 018 — Domain realization context boundary
940-
941-**Status**
942-
943-Added by `cycle-018-wave-plan-extension` as the recommended next wave after Wave 017. Requires `cycle-018-wave-plan-extension-review` sign-off before the canonical `cycle-018-fresh-scout-proposals` stage and before any implementation.
944-
945-**Scope**
946-
947-- `frontend/src/domain/world/projectionPlane/ProjectionPlaneContext.ts`
948-- `frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts`
949-- `frontend/src/domain/world/Element3D.ts`
950-- 3D realization classes that still type realization against concrete `World` or `any`:
951-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Point3D.ts`
952-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Line3D.ts`
953-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Segment3D.ts`
954-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Plane.ts`
955-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/HingeLine.ts`
956-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/BrokenHingeLine.ts`
957-- 2D realization classes only where needed to align naming/types with the existing projection-element context:
958-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Point.ts`
959-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Line.ts`
960-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Segment.ts`
961-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Circle.ts`
962-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/Guide.ts`
963-  - `frontend/src/domain/world/elements/BrokenHalfHingeLine2D.ts`
964-- Presentation read-port adapters that currently pass concrete `World` into domain realization:
965-  - `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts`
966-  - `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts`
967-- focused realization-context, canvas-read-port, three-read-port, and representative rendering tests
968-
969-**Scope guard**
970-
971-This wave owns the domain realization context contract, not a broad rendering, scene-host, command, persistence, app-shell, backend, validation-platform, docs/spec, or package/tooling redesign. It must begin with a current caller inventory for `realize2D(...)`, `realize3D(...)`, `getPlaneEquation(...)`, and projection-plane realization helper APIs, then choose the smallest typed context boundary that removes concrete `World`/`any` from active realization contracts without introducing a new god context.
972-
973-Do not reopen the Wave 016/017 presentation selector read-port architecture except to update adapters to the new realization context. Do not move ownership of style, visibility, process-tree rendering, command execution, or persistence into the realization context. If the caller inventory proves that projection-plane mutation APIs or dependency registration must be redesigned first, stop and run a reviewed plan-edit mini-cycle rather than hiding that redesign in this wave.
974-
975-**Baseline/current grounding**
976-
977-The baseline already identified domain-internal realization coupling as a residual central risk: `Element2D` required realization through a whole `World`, `styleService` walked `World`/`ProcessTree`, and weak realization contexts used `any` (`architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md`, R6 and R11; `architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md`, “Additional service/domain coupling paths”). Waves 016 and 017 deliberately narrowed canvas and 3D presentation selectors to read ports, but both closure logs record the same residual: presentation read-port adapters still call domain realization APIs with concrete runtime `World` (`architecture-audit/cycle-016-canvas-presentation-overlay-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Residual risks / future candidates”; `architecture-audit/cycle-017-three-presentation-read-port-realization-boundary/implementation-log.md`, “Residual risks after closure”).
978-
979-Current source evidence confirms that the residual is now a domain-realization boundary, not a selector-boundary problem. `CanvasWorldReadPort` exposes realization methods and its adapter calls `plane.realizePoint2D(point, world)`, `plane.realizeLine2D(line, world)`, `plane.realizeCircle2D(circle, world)`, `point.realize3D(world)`, `line.realize3D(world)`, and `segment.realize3D(world)` (`frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts:14`, `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts:21`, `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts:30`, `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts:46`, `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts:51`). `ThreeWorldReadPort` similarly wraps `World` and builds read models by calling `point.realize2D(world)`, `line.realize2D(world)`, `circle.realize2D(world)`, selected-guide `line.realize2D(world)`, and hinge `realize3D(world)` inside the adapter (`frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts:55`, `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts:65`, `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts:84`, `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts:98`, `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/ThreeWorldReadPort.ts:117`).
980-
981-The domain has already started the right vocabulary for 2D realization with `ProjectionElementRealizationContext` (`frontend/src/domain/world/projectionPlane/ProjectionPlaneContext.ts:9`, `frontend/src/domain/world/projectionPlane/ProjectionPlaneContext.ts:20`), and `Element2D.realize2D(context: ProjectionElementRealizationContext)` now uses that type (`frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts:1`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts:108`). The remaining central weakness is that 3D realization and plane-equation contracts still use concrete `World` or `any`: `Element3D.realize3D(world: any): any` (`frontend/src/domain/world/Element3D.ts:40`), `Point3D`/`Line3D`/`Segment3D` import `World` for realization (`frontend/src/domain/world/Point3D.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Line3D.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Segment3D.ts`), and `Plane` uses `any` in plane-equation/realization APIs (`frontend/src/domain/world/Plane.ts`). Static scans in `architecture-audit/cycle-018-wave-plan-extension/static-realization-world-scan.stdout` and `static-any-scan.stdout` capture the current residual seams.
982-
983-**Target outcome**
984-
985-Domain realization APIs consume explicit typed realization/read contexts rather than full mutable `World` or broad `any`. 2D and 3D realization share a coherent context vocabulary where their lookup needs overlap, with separate narrow capabilities where they do not. Canvas and three presentation read-port adapters may still be the runtime boundary that wraps a concrete `World`, but they pass only the selected realization context into domain realization APIs. The active source no longer has a parallel situation where selectors use read ports while domain realization contracts force adapters back to full `World`/`any`.
986-
987-**Explicit DELETE list**
988-
989-- Delete `Element3D.realize3D(world: any): any` and replace it with a typed 3D realization context/result contract.
990-- Delete `Plane.getPlaneEquation(world: any)` / `Plane.realize3D(world: any)` broad `any` contracts in touched plane classes.
991-- Delete concrete `World` realization signatures from active 3D domain elements where a typed context is sufficient, including point/line/segment/plane/hinge realization paths covered by the caller inventory.
992-- Delete presentation adapter calls that pass full `World` directly to `realize2D(...)`, `realize3D(...)`, or plane-equation APIs when the new context is available.
993-- Delete redundant realization-context names or shims if implementation discovers the existing `ProjectionElementRealizationContext` can be evolved cleanly instead of duplicated.
994-- Delete touched unit-test helper `as any`/broad mock contexts that only exist because realization contracts are weak; replace with typed test context builders.
995-- Delete transitional overloads, compatibility wrappers, dead exports, and type aliases that preserve both old full-`World` and new context APIs.
996-
997-**Success criteria**
998-
999-- A caller inventory in `implementation-log.md` lists active `realize2D`, `realize3D`, `getPlaneEquation`, projection-plane realization helper, and presentation-read-port adapter call sites before edits and states which are changed, deferred, or explicitly out of scope.
1000-- Active 3D realization base contracts no longer use `any` or concrete `World` where a typed realization context is sufficient.
1001-- Existing 2D `ProjectionElementRealizationContext` usage is preserved or evolved into a clearly named realization context family; no second duplicate context is introduced for the same lookup responsibility.
1002-- `CanvasWorldReadPort` and `ThreeWorldReadPort` pass typed realization contexts into domain realization calls rather than exposing selector-side read ports that internally depend on full-`World` realization signatures.
1003-- Focused tests cover the selected realization context using typed test fixtures for representative 2D point/line/circle/guide, 3D point/line/segment/plane/hinge, and canvas/three read-port adapter paths changed by the wave.
1004-- No source change is made to command/undo, persistence/project schema, app-shell orchestration, backend contracts, package/tooling, docs/specs, Drive/local services, or broad rendering/scene-host modules except if a reviewed mini-cycle explicitly broadens scope.
1005-- Mandatory validation cadence passes with stable logs: root/frontend lint where defined, focused Vitest for realization/read-port tests, full root/frontend Vitest, root/frontend build, root/frontend e2e because canvas/3D rendering is user-observable, live preview refresh on `0.0.0.0:5173`, HTTP reachability probe, and Playwright/live smoke for representative 2D canvas plus 3D view rendering.
1006-
1007-**Dependencies**
1008-
1009-Depends on Waves 016 and 017 because those waves moved presentation selectors behind canvas/three read ports and exposed the remaining full-`World` seam as a domain realization issue. It is ordered before broader 3D scene-host lifecycle, app-shell service concentration, backend/frontend contract stance, validation-gate hardening beyond existing gates, placeholder/debug cleanup, and docs/spec drift because those later topics should consume a stable domain realization/read-context contract rather than preserve the current full-`World` realization API.
1010-
1011-**Validation requirements**
1012-
1013-1. Capture pre-edit static scans for `realize2D`, `realize3D`, `getPlaneEquation`, `World` imports in realization classes, `any` realization contracts, and read-port adapter calls that pass full `World` into realization.
1014-2. Run focused Vitest for changed realization context/domain element/read-port adapter modules.
1015-3. Run root and frontend lint where scripts exist.
1016-4. Run full root and frontend Vitest.
1017-5. Run root and frontend build.
1018-6. Run root and frontend Playwright e2e because realization affects user-visible 2D/3D rendering, construction, intersections, guides, and projection-plane behavior.
1019-7. Refresh the live preview on `0.0.0.0:5173`, capture HTTP 200, and run focused Playwright/live browser smoke that confirms representative 2D canvas primitives and the 3D view still render.
